### 1. Get all tasks
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks


### 2. Get a single task
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks/1


### 3. Get a task that does not exist
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks/999

### 4. Create a new task with valid data
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Finish Assignment 1",
  "description": "Complete and test the REST API assignment",
  "user_id": 1,
  "completed": false
}


### 5. Create a task with missing title
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "This should fail because title is missing",
  "user_id": 1
}


### 6. Create a task with invalid user_id
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Invalid User Test",
  "description": "This should fail because user 999 does not exist",
  "user_id": 999,
  "completed": false
}

### 7. Update an existing task
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn REST Updated",
  "completed": false
}


### 8. Delete a task
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks/2


### 9. Get tasks for a specific user
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/users/1/tasks